# Ground effects under the creatures (client/BASE.md 0055): an effect id registered with g_map.setGroundEffect(id, true) is drawn after the bottom layer and before every creature, like a decal on the floor, instead of above the creatures. A big effect reaches up and left of its tile into tiles drawn before it, so with GameMapDrawGroundFirst the first tile it covers draws it (the walls and items of later tiles still go over it); in the negative-offset layer pass it is queued after every bottom layer. Tile::drawTop skips those ids. Lua: g_map.setGroundEffect(id, on), g_map.isGroundEffect(id), g_map.clearGroundEffects(). The overlay module game_townportal registers the Town Portal channel circle (effect 744) (live test winpkg-35: the portal pad covered the character). C++ only.
